        an inseparable contractual whole with these terms and conditions.</p>
      <p>MALFUNCTION(S): functional anomaly/anomalies affecting the use of IZIKA to varying
        degrees.</p>
      <p>INTERNET: open, informal network formed by the international interconnection of computer
        networks using the TCP/IP standard, whose management is not subject to any central
        authority, each portion of this network belonging either to a public, private or
        independent organisation. Its operation relies on cooperation between the operators of the
        various networks, with no obligation of supply or quality of supply between operators. The
        networks may have unequal transmission capacities and their own usage policies. No one can
        guarantee the proper functioning of the Internet as a whole.</p>
      <p>BEST-EFFORTS OBLIGATION: contractual commitment requiring the party bound by it to deploy
        the most effective means and techniques known at the date of signature of the agreement to
        achieve the result set by the contract.</p>
      <p>SOFTWARE: the set of programs, processes, rules and documentation relating to the
        operation of a data processing system (French order of 22.12.1981 on the enrichment of IT
        vocabulary – Official Journal of 17.01.1982).</p>
      <p>WEB BROWSER: software designed to view WEB content.</p>
      <p>OPERATOR: Internet access provider.</p>
      <p>OS: operating system: internal software of a computing device allowing its operation and
        the running of third-party software.</p>
      <p>SAAS: (software as a service) software application accessible remotely, as a service, via
        the WEB.</p>
      <p>SERVER(S): hardware or software computing device providing access to certain services,
        whether accessible via the Web or not.</p>
      <p>APPLICATION SERVICE(S): service available online on subscription, allowing the use of
        software whose hosting, management and maintenance are handled by the service provider.</p>
      <p>WEBSITE: a set of organised pages intended to be published on the WEB under a single
        domain name.</p>
      <p>URL: Uniform resource locator: the location of a digital resource on the Web.</p>
      <p>APPENDIX: binding contractual document attached to the CONTRACT</p>
      <p>WEB: or World Wide Web: system based on hypertext links using the http protocol (hyper
        text transfer protocol) allowing the content of pages on the Internet to be viewed.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="article-3">
      <h2>Article 3. PURPOSE</h2>
      <p>IZIKA makes available to the Customer, who accepts it, a set of services including, among
        others and without this being exhaustive or binding for IZIKA, a right of access to the
        features of the IZIKA SOFTWARE and a right to use said application SERVICES in accordance
        with the terms and conditions set out below.</p>
      <p>The IZIKA software allows the CUSTOMER's electronic calendars (Google or iCAL calendars,
        without limitation) to be connected to a mapping and calculation system that extracts the
        appointments from the electronic calendars linked to Google accounts (or other providers),
        computes the distances travelled, and estimates the time spent driving, the average fuel
        consumption and the CO2 (carbon dioxide) emissions.</p>
      <p>This software is provided without any warranty of accuracy regarding the mileage,
        duration, fuel consumption or CO2 emission values.</p>
      <p>It is the customer's responsibility to check the appointment summary table themselves,
        verifying the validity of each appointment (its accounting justification), the departure
        and arrival addresses, the computed mileage as well as the time, fuel and CO2 data.</p>
    </section>

